WEBVTT

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:09.410
This is it!

00:00:09.410 --> 00:00:11.400
A completely round-looking line.

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:13.750
The C-cup I had always wanted!

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:15.760
I wish it could stay this way forever.

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:17.470
You’re at it again?

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:21.860
Hurry up. We’re going to be late.

00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:23.090
Okay.

00:00:23.090 --> 00:00:26.170
Irie-kun, do you think you’ll be able to go to Kin-chan’s place tonight?

00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:29.190
Ah, sorry. I don’t think I can.

00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:30.470
Send my regards.

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:32.490
Wait!

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:38.550
Okay!

00:00:48.650 --> 00:00:50.150
Amazing.

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:52.070
They’re all royalty.

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:54.910
Kinnosuke was very manly, wasn’t he?

00:00:56.850 --> 00:00:59.330
I wish Irie-kun could see these too.

00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:01.510
Has Irie been busy lately?

00:01:01.510 --> 00:01:04.770
Yeah. The deadline for his thesis is coming up.

00:01:04.770 --> 00:01:07.340
Looks like the genius is having it rough.

00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:09.050
Here’s some water, Kotoko.

00:01:09.050 --> 00:01:10.170
Thanks.

00:01:12.550 --> 00:01:15.570
Why are you taking that medicine?
Are you ill?

00:01:15.570 --> 00:01:17.180
No, these are iron supplements.

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:20.000
Ah, for replenishing your
red blood cells, right?

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:23.380
I heard that pregnant women were susceptible to anemia.

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:25.480
Oh, really?

00:01:26.410 --> 00:01:29.110
Careful of anemia. Take iron.

00:01:29.110 --> 00:01:30.640
What are you doing?

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:33.400
I’m gathering information.

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:34.070
Information?

00:01:35.910 --> 00:01:40.910
Actually, I was told that I’m already three months pregnant when I visited the hospital.

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:43.410
Chris, you’re pregnant too?

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:47.310
Congratulations! Good for you!

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:48.860
Congratulations, Kin-chan!

00:01:48.860 --> 00:01:49.550
Thanks.

00:01:49.550 --> 00:01:52.120
Look! Aren’t they pretty?

00:01:54.140 --> 00:01:56.630
How adorable! Did you knit them?

00:01:56.630 --> 00:01:59.720
Why blue? It might be a girl.

00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:04.400
No! It will be a handsome boy who looks just like his father.

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:07.110
I think it would be happier looking like the mother.

00:02:07.110 --> 00:02:10.810
Kin-chan, you sure found yourself
a great wife.

00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:13.110
Anyway, let’s have another toast!

00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:15.320
Cheers!

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:18.620
And then, I heard that he’s been fighting with Chris’s mother again...

00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:22.070
...over whether to have the baby delivered in Japan or England.

00:02:22.070 --> 00:02:25.800
International weddings sure are difficult, aren’t they?

00:02:31.160 --> 00:02:32.370
That’s right.

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:35.240
This is a tough period for him.

00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:37.730
What’s wrong?

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:41.730
Is your thesis progressing well?

00:02:41.730 --> 00:02:43.090
I guess.

00:02:43.090 --> 00:02:45.730
You didn’t sleep that much yesterday, did you?

00:02:45.730 --> 00:02:47.320
Don’t overwork yourself, okay?

00:02:47.320 --> 00:02:48.980
Yeah. Thank you.

00:02:53.030 --> 00:02:53.860
Kotoko?

00:02:53.860 --> 00:02:54.970
Are you all right?

00:02:58.470 --> 00:03:00.140
My hand slipped.

00:03:00.140 --> 00:03:01.270
Be careful.

00:03:01.270 --> 00:03:04.020
Okay. Sorry for disturbing you.

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:05.270
Good luck.

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:21.970
Kotoko-san, are you okay with those?

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:23.710
I’m fine.

00:03:23.710 --> 00:03:25.460
Don’t overwork yourself.

00:03:25.460 --> 00:03:28.100
You haven’t applied for maternity leave yet?

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:31.440
No. I was thinking of working as long as I can.

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:32.730
I love my work after all.

00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:36.960
Kotoko, have you been influenced by that lady president?

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:39.370
You know, the one who got
admitted last year.

00:03:39.370 --> 00:03:40.370
Matsumoto-san?

00:03:40.370 --> 00:03:43.870
Speaking of which, what happened between her and that sempai?

00:03:43.870 --> 00:03:46.980
Yeah. That clumsy, moustached salesman.

00:03:46.980 --> 00:03:49.740
It seems that he was elevated to boyfriend status after her discharge.

00:03:49.740 --> 00:03:51.460
Oh, well done.

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:54.320
I wonder how Matsumoto-san is doing.

00:03:55.020 --> 00:03:57.310
Has she been getting her checkups?

00:03:57.310 --> 00:03:59.640
Duodenal ulcers are prone
to relapse, after all.

00:04:01.390 --> 00:04:03.920
It’s Kobayashi-san. I’ll get it.

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:07.610
Okay then, Kotoko-san. We’ll be leaving first.

00:04:07.610 --> 00:04:08.850
Good work.

00:04:08.850 --> 00:04:10.790
Good work!

00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:17.570
My stomach hurts...

00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:20.230
Did I take too many iron supplements?

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:25.510
Your thesis, huh? Don’t overdo it, okay?

00:04:25.510 --> 00:04:26.370
Right.

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:27.920
I’ll be going then.

00:04:27.920 --> 00:04:29.090
Good work.

00:04:29.090 --> 00:04:31.810
Oh, Kotoko-chan. Here to pick him up?

00:04:31.810 --> 00:04:34.370
Dr. Nishigaki. Good work.

00:04:35.810 --> 00:04:38.100
Irie-kun. Let’s go home together.

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:40.930
Ah, sorry, but I don’t think
I’ll be finishing soon.

00:04:40.930 --> 00:04:42.210
Oh, really?

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:45.790
It’s going to take a while,
so you can go home first.

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:51.000
I understand. Good luck then.

00:05:00.710 --> 00:05:03.230
I feel a little lightheaded...

00:05:03.230 --> 00:05:05.910
Dr. Kurihara. Sorry for calling so late.

00:05:05.910 --> 00:05:07.970
I’d like to ask for your opinion...

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:20.090
I feel sick...

00:05:24.430 --> 00:05:27.000
What should I do? It really hurts.

00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:29.220
Irie-kun.

00:05:30.460 --> 00:05:32.350
Excuse me. Are you all right?

00:05:33.180 --> 00:05:34.070
Yes.

00:05:37.500 --> 00:05:40.090
What’s wrong? Hang in there!

00:05:53.480 --> 00:05:54.850
Onii-chan!

00:05:58.120 --> 00:05:58.570
Kotoko!

00:05:58.570 --> 00:05:59.580
Kotoko-chan!
Kotoko!

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:05.260
Kotoko! Hang in there!

00:06:05.260 --> 00:06:07.530
Kotoko!

00:06:13.110 --> 00:06:14.390
Kotoko-chan.

00:06:14.390 --> 00:06:15.140
Kotoko!

00:06:17.880 --> 00:06:20.070
Kotoko, are you all right?

00:06:21.660 --> 00:06:22.670
Irie-kun.

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:26.200
Kotoko-chan. Thank goodness.

00:06:30.780 --> 00:06:33.350
Don’t worry. The baby is safe.

00:06:34.940 --> 00:06:36.420
Thank goodness.

00:06:37.470 --> 00:06:38.810
Umm, I...

00:06:38.810 --> 00:06:41.620
They said it was just
pregnancy hypertension.

00:06:41.620 --> 00:06:44.770
But, it’s minor,
so there’s no need to worry.

00:06:45.390 --> 00:06:49.260
They said you should take maternity leave and rest at home after this.

00:06:49.260 --> 00:06:50.790
I see.

00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:54.210
Yeah. You overworked yourself.

00:06:54.210 --> 00:06:58.400
Either way, I’m glad both you and the baby are safe.

00:06:58.400 --> 00:07:00.810
Sorry for worrying you all.

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:04.150
Dad, that’s...?

00:07:06.210 --> 00:07:07.690
I was in a rush.

00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:10.170
You’ve always been such a scatterbrain.

00:07:10.170 --> 00:07:12.540
What about yourself?

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:18.170
Oh dear, Papa.

00:07:18.170 --> 00:07:20.540
You shouldn’t be talking
about others, Mama.

00:07:20.540 --> 00:07:22.120
What’s that on your head?

00:07:36.550 --> 00:07:37.770
Onii-chan.

00:07:38.450 --> 00:07:40.630
Mama and the others said they’re going home soon.

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:42.490
I see.

00:07:43.460 --> 00:07:47.020
Kotoko sure likes causing false alarms.

00:07:47.930 --> 00:07:50.100
But, I’m glad she’s all right.

00:07:51.190 --> 00:07:53.370
She’s probably been enduring it
the whole time...

00:07:53.840 --> 00:07:56.890
...forcing herself to act normally so as to avoid worrying me.

00:07:57.720 --> 00:07:59.080
I’m a failure as her husband.

00:08:01.210 --> 00:08:03.190
You’ve changed.

00:08:04.360 --> 00:08:07.200
You were always so composed in the past.

00:08:08.010 --> 00:08:11.470
I’ve always admired you because of that.

00:08:11.470 --> 00:08:12.680
Did I disappoint you?

00:08:13.640 --> 00:08:14.720
No.

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:18.150
I think you’re better the way you are now.

00:08:20.730 --> 00:08:23.320
Let’s go. Kotoko is waiting.

00:08:28.610 --> 00:08:29.840
What are you doing?

00:08:31.900 --> 00:08:37.570
Well, I wanted to knit some booties just like Chris, but...

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:39.500
Geez, what a klutz.

00:08:39.500 --> 00:08:43.550
The way you said that was just like how Irie-kun says it!

00:08:43.550 --> 00:08:45.460
As expected from brothers.

00:08:48.020 --> 00:08:50.130
I’m sorry, Kotoko.

00:08:51.280 --> 00:08:53.890
I failed to notice your health.

00:08:53.890 --> 00:08:59.130
No, me too. I shouldn’t have overworked myself and instead told you about it.

00:09:00.280 --> 00:09:02.860
I heard your voice.

00:09:03.770 --> 00:09:06.980
You repeatedly called out
my name, didn’t you?

00:09:08.410 --> 00:09:09.830
It was very reassuring.

00:09:11.250 --> 00:09:14.380
It made me feel that you were with me.

00:09:15.290 --> 00:09:20.570
Hey, Irie-kun. When I give birth to the baby, will you be with me too?

00:09:20.570 --> 00:09:21.350
Yes.

00:09:21.350 --> 00:09:22.210
Really?

00:09:22.820 --> 00:09:25.080
I’ll be there. I promise.

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:27.060
Thank goodness.

00:09:27.060 --> 00:09:30.510
They say there are many people who panic during childbirth.

00:09:30.510 --> 00:09:33.470
I would be very disheartened if I had to do it alone.

00:09:33.470 --> 00:09:35.010
Thank you.

00:09:39.330 --> 00:09:40.930
Go ahead. Please take your time.

00:09:52.700 --> 00:09:54.990
You’re doing it wrong, Kotoko-chan.

00:09:54.990 --> 00:09:57.470
You have to move your hands more fluidly, like this.

00:09:58.050 --> 00:10:01.050
Okay. Like this?

00:10:02.290 --> 00:10:03.800
That’s completely wrong!

00:10:03.800 --> 00:10:06.060
Straighten your back, Papa!

00:10:07.030 --> 00:10:08.880
This sure is difficult.

00:10:09.360 --> 00:10:10.450
I’m home.

00:10:11.300 --> 00:10:12.880
What are you all up to?

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:14.950
Maternity hula.

00:10:14.950 --> 00:10:16.540
It’s good for the body.

00:10:16.540 --> 00:10:18.910
Would you like to join us?

00:10:18.910 --> 00:10:19.890
I’ll pass.

00:10:19.890 --> 00:10:22.720
But, it’s so much fun.

00:10:22.720 --> 00:10:23.930
Right, Papa?

00:10:27.340 --> 00:10:31.970
Say, Irie-kun. Chris invited us to this.

00:10:33.790 --> 00:10:35.540
Maternity Class?

00:10:36.940 --> 00:10:41.790
You wouldn’t go to such a thing, right?

00:10:42.840 --> 00:10:47.230
It’s okay. It seems like a lot of husbands aren’t going to make it.

00:10:47.230 --> 00:10:48.440
I can go on my own.

00:10:48.440 --> 00:10:49.410
Sure, I’ll go.

00:10:50.530 --> 00:10:51.850
Really?

00:10:52.280 --> 00:10:54.110
Hooray! Thank you!

00:10:54.110 --> 00:10:55.780
Onii-chan, well done!

00:10:56.340 --> 00:10:58.610
While you’re at it,
why don’t you hula with us too?

00:10:58.610 --> 00:10:59.540
No, thanks.

00:10:59.540 --> 00:11:00.870
Oh, really?

00:11:03.970 --> 00:11:05.060
I see.

00:11:06.640 --> 00:11:09.850
It’s heavy, isn’t it?
There’s at least eight kilos.

00:11:10.850 --> 00:11:11.780
Kin-chan?

00:11:11.780 --> 00:11:15.040
Kinnosuke, what’s wrong?

00:11:15.040 --> 00:11:19.200
I don’t know,
but I feel these beautiful feelings!

00:11:23.160 --> 00:11:26.640
As expected from Irie-kun.
He’s good at anything he does.

00:11:26.640 --> 00:11:27.340
How wonderful!

00:11:27.340 --> 00:11:29.080
I’m so jealous that you have such a handsome husband!

00:11:30.230 --> 00:11:33.530
Sheesh, cleaning the baby is a piece of cake for me too.

00:11:33.530 --> 00:11:36.800
Oh, Kinnosuke, the baby is drowning!

00:11:42.970 --> 00:11:46.270
I’m a professional at this, so I won’t lose to anyone.

00:11:50.350 --> 00:11:52.440
You’re right. It’s really delicious.

00:11:55.290 --> 00:11:56.880
How is it?

00:11:56.880 --> 00:11:58.350
Why don’t you try tasting it?

00:12:02.450 --> 00:12:05.580
Kotoko, let me try it too, please.

00:12:07.170 --> 00:12:08.450
Are you okay?

00:12:08.450 --> 00:12:13.460
I’ll start practicing from now on so that I can make really tasty food.

00:12:14.120 --> 00:12:15.290
What’s wrong?

00:12:15.290 --> 00:12:18.200
My stomach just suddenly contracted...

00:12:18.200 --> 00:12:20.420
Was it that bad?

00:12:20.420 --> 00:12:21.740
It’s not that.

00:12:23.650 --> 00:12:25.270
Don’t tell me, you’re...

00:12:25.270 --> 00:12:26.710
...going into labor?

00:12:27.820 --> 00:12:28.890
Hey, Kotoko!

00:12:36.210 --> 00:12:39.590
Please inform me when the gaps between the contractions shorten.

00:12:39.590 --> 00:12:40.830
Okay.

00:12:40.830 --> 00:12:42.850
It’s finally time, Kotoko-chan.

00:12:42.850 --> 00:12:46.080
Remember, breathe. <i>Hee</i>, <i>hee</i>, <i>huu</i>.

00:12:47.120 --> 00:12:48.370
What should I do?

00:12:48.950 --> 00:12:50.830
I’m starting to feel scared.

00:12:50.830 --> 00:12:52.870
Be strong.

00:12:52.870 --> 00:12:54.390
You’re going to become a mother, right?

00:12:56.760 --> 00:12:57.920
But...

00:12:57.920 --> 00:12:59.090
I’ll be here with you.

00:13:01.380 --> 00:13:03.790
That’s true. I’ll give it my best.

00:13:04.530 --> 00:13:07.170
Ah, Yuuki-kun. You came.

00:13:07.170 --> 00:13:09.720
What’s this?
Looks like nothing has happened yet.

00:13:10.040 --> 00:13:13.080
Labor pains come in cycles.

00:13:14.050 --> 00:13:15.450
Is it here?

00:13:20.650 --> 00:13:24.340
You can’t fight on an empty stomach, right?

00:13:24.340 --> 00:13:25.990
Make sure you don’t eat too much.

00:13:27.090 --> 00:13:29.300
This one looks really tasty too!

00:13:29.300 --> 00:13:31.710
Kotoko-chan, which drink would you like?

00:13:31.710 --> 00:13:33.690
Matsumoto!

00:13:34.900 --> 00:13:37.340
Matsumoto, hang in there!

00:13:37.340 --> 00:13:39.170
Matsumoto-san?

00:13:39.170 --> 00:13:40.450
I’m going to take a look.

00:13:41.460 --> 00:13:42.630
Sudou-san!

00:13:42.630 --> 00:13:45.670
Irie! Matsumoto...!

00:13:45.670 --> 00:13:47.330
Tell me what happened!

00:13:47.330 --> 00:13:50.270
She was on the floor when I went to pick her up from the office.

00:13:50.270 --> 00:13:52.770
Blood... She was coughing up a lot of blood.

00:13:52.770 --> 00:13:53.770
She was unconscious!

00:13:54.340 --> 00:13:55.520
Please stay calm.

00:13:55.520 --> 00:13:59.290
Dr. Irie. There are no available doctors at the moment.

00:13:59.290 --> 00:14:00.520
Can you look at her?

00:14:00.520 --> 00:14:02.510
Where’s Dr. Nishigaki?

00:14:02.510 --> 00:14:05.310
He just entered into an emergency operation.

00:14:05.310 --> 00:14:06.280
Understood.

00:14:06.770 --> 00:14:09.890
Matsumoto!

00:14:11.360 --> 00:14:12.410
Where are her records?

00:14:12.410 --> 00:14:13.420
Here.

00:14:14.740 --> 00:14:16.490
Prepare her for an x-ray.

00:14:16.490 --> 00:14:17.500
Yes.

00:14:18.080 --> 00:14:19.870
How worrying.

00:14:19.870 --> 00:14:22.200
Onii-chan hasn’t returned either.

00:14:23.010 --> 00:14:25.510
Let’s go back to the room in the meantime.

00:14:26.620 --> 00:14:27.830
Kotoko-chan?

00:14:28.510 --> 00:14:31.670
Looks like a badly perforated duodenal ulcer.

00:14:31.670 --> 00:14:35.520
There’s a lot of visible hemorrhaging.
It’ll be risky if we don’t operate right away.

00:14:35.520 --> 00:14:36.800
Where’s Dr. Nishigaki?

00:14:36.800 --> 00:14:38.020
He’s still in surgery.

00:14:38.020 --> 00:14:39.950
Then, call Dr. Suzuki.

00:14:39.950 --> 00:14:43.870
I tried calling him earlier,
but he didn’t pick up.

00:14:43.870 --> 00:14:45.460
This isn’t good...

00:14:45.460 --> 00:14:47.560
Dr. Matsuda is attending an academic meeting.

00:14:47.560 --> 00:14:49.950
In that case, why don’t we have Dr. Irie perform it?

00:14:49.950 --> 00:14:53.270
Dr. Irie has only assisted in operations before.

00:14:53.270 --> 00:14:54.820
He won’t be able to be the lead surgeon.

00:14:55.760 --> 00:14:57.830
But, at this rate...

00:14:59.680 --> 00:15:03.060
Please confirm the status of Dr. Nishigaki’s operation once more.

00:15:03.060 --> 00:15:03.950
Yes.

00:15:03.950 --> 00:15:08.190
Chief Nurse, can you try contacting Dr. Sekiguchi from Keime Medical University?

00:15:08.190 --> 00:15:09.510
Got it.

00:15:12.770 --> 00:15:14.320
Her blood pressure is falling!

00:15:15.610 --> 00:15:17.850
When fully powered, ready the emergency blood transfusion.

00:15:17.850 --> 00:15:21.470
Dr. Nishigaki will take
another two to three hours.

00:15:21.470 --> 00:15:23.760
Try Dr. Suzuki again.

00:15:23.760 --> 00:15:25.040
Got it!

00:15:26.410 --> 00:15:29.320
Dr. Sekiguchi is overseas on business.

00:15:29.320 --> 00:15:31.830
Blood pressure has dropped to 80.

00:15:31.830 --> 00:15:33.940
Her pulse is weak and is at 150 beats.

00:15:33.940 --> 00:15:36.270
Emergency transfusion via pumping!

00:15:36.270 --> 00:15:37.000
Yes.

00:15:39.220 --> 00:15:40.500
Save her.

00:15:44.660 --> 00:15:45.550
Kotoko?

00:15:46.720 --> 00:15:48.470
Why are you here?

00:15:50.220 --> 00:15:52.550
Save Matsumoto-san.

00:15:53.670 --> 00:15:57.170
It’ll be okay. I’m sure you can do it.

00:15:58.640 --> 00:16:00.320
I’ll do my best too.

00:16:00.320 --> 00:16:02.330
So, you too, Irie-kun.

00:16:03.310 --> 00:16:04.700
Let’s do our best.

00:16:08.200 --> 00:16:10.110
Prepare her for surgery.

00:16:14.420 --> 00:16:15.950
I’ll be the lead surgeon.

00:16:16.480 --> 00:16:17.580
Irie-kun.

00:16:17.580 --> 00:16:20.050
A word, if I may.

00:16:20.050 --> 00:16:23.190
You’ve barely gone independent.

00:16:23.190 --> 00:16:25.680
Though I may be a novice, I’m still a doctor.

00:16:25.680 --> 00:16:29.640
I can’t ignore a patient whose life is in danger.

00:16:29.640 --> 00:16:30.210
But...!

00:16:30.650 --> 00:16:32.930
Head nurse, please believe in Irie-kun!

00:16:32.930 --> 00:16:36.060
He <i>will</i> succeed.

00:16:38.540 --> 00:16:40.870
Kikyou-san, arrange the operation.

00:16:40.870 --> 00:16:41.920
Chief Nurse!

00:16:41.920 --> 00:16:44.360
Shimizu-san, contact the
anesthesiology department!

00:16:45.610 --> 00:16:46.850
Right away!

00:16:47.780 --> 00:16:49.800
Hello? Anesthesiology?

00:16:50.770 --> 00:16:53.060
Matsumoto, do your best!

00:16:53.060 --> 00:16:55.530
It’ll be okay. Irie <i>will</i> save you!

00:16:55.530 --> 00:16:57.490
Do your best, okay?

00:16:58.970 --> 00:17:01.670
I’m sorry that I can’t be with you.

00:17:02.310 --> 00:17:03.440
It’s okay.

00:17:03.980 --> 00:17:07.440
I’m sure the baby is cheering Papa on.

00:17:07.980 --> 00:17:09.470
Saying, “Do your best.”

00:17:11.750 --> 00:17:12.880
Dr. Irie.

00:17:13.920 --> 00:17:16.930
Mother, please take care of Kotoko.

00:17:16.930 --> 00:17:19.140
Leave it to me.

00:17:19.140 --> 00:17:21.030
I’m going now, then.

00:17:21.620 --> 00:17:23.170
Irie, please!

00:17:23.170 --> 00:17:24.140
Yes!

00:17:26.280 --> 00:17:27.440
Are you okay?

00:17:27.440 --> 00:17:28.490
Yes.

00:17:28.490 --> 00:17:30.660
Kotoko-chan, <i>hee</i>, <i>hee</i>, <i>huu!</i>

00:17:37.070 --> 00:17:42.360
We shall now commence the operation to close the perforated ulcer on the duodenum.

00:17:43.480 --> 00:17:46.300
Kotoko-chan, just hang in there
a little longer.

00:17:47.870 --> 00:17:49.040
Yes.

00:17:50.130 --> 00:17:53.000
That’s right. I have to try my best.

00:17:53.000 --> 00:17:55.800
Irie-kun is trying his best after all.

00:17:56.420 --> 00:18:00.270
Our baby will be born soon, won’t it?

00:18:00.890 --> 00:18:05.020
I never thought this day
would come back then.

00:18:05.530 --> 00:18:06.270
Please accept...

00:18:06.270 --> 00:18:07.190
I don’t want it.

00:18:07.190 --> 00:18:09.690
Please don’t cramp my lifestyle.

00:18:12.000 --> 00:18:13.900
You love me!

00:18:13.900 --> 00:18:15.490
You won’t be able to love anyone else!

00:18:17.670 --> 00:18:19.420
Serves you right.

00:18:20.460 --> 00:18:22.440
Hey, Irie-kun...

00:18:23.260 --> 00:18:25.500
Falling in love is amazing, isn’t it?

00:18:26.640 --> 00:18:30.140
It can turn a mundane life into a jewel.

00:18:31.030 --> 00:18:34.020
Loving someone is amazing, isn’t it?

00:18:35.090 --> 00:18:37.790
Just a bit more. Do your best!

00:18:38.410 --> 00:18:39.570
Irie-kun!

00:18:45.870 --> 00:18:46.800
Irie!

00:18:48.080 --> 00:18:48.940
How’s Matsumoto?

00:18:50.140 --> 00:18:51.860
The surgery was a success.

00:18:54.920 --> 00:18:55.870
Thank you!

00:18:56.630 --> 00:18:58.450
Thank you!

00:18:58.450 --> 00:19:02.030
Dr. Irie, we’ll manage from here.

00:19:02.030 --> 00:19:03.660
Go to Kotoko, quickly.

00:19:07.310 --> 00:19:07.950
Naoki-kun!

00:19:08.650 --> 00:19:09.600
Onii-chan!

00:19:22.150 --> 00:19:23.870
You can finally meet him.

00:19:23.870 --> 00:19:27.440
Papa and Mama have been waiting for you all this time.

00:19:28.560 --> 00:19:30.440
Your Papa is amazing, you know?

00:19:31.240 --> 00:19:34.770
He saved a friend’s life
then came rushing over.

00:19:35.350 --> 00:19:36.670
Well done.

00:19:36.670 --> 00:19:37.660
Irie-kun.

00:19:38.730 --> 00:19:40.090
Hold her.

00:19:49.380 --> 00:19:51.160
Thank you, Kotoko.

00:19:56.170 --> 00:19:59.090
Congratulations, Kotoko-chan, Onii-chan.

00:20:00.020 --> 00:20:02.140
Kotoko, you did well.

00:20:02.140 --> 00:20:03.750
Congratulations.

00:20:03.750 --> 00:20:05.050
You did it.

00:20:07.590 --> 00:20:09.560
Okay, I’m going to take it.

00:20:16.140 --> 00:20:19.400
Kotomi! Wait!

00:20:19.400 --> 00:20:21.850
Wait, Kotomi!

00:20:21.850 --> 00:20:23.560
Wear your hat!

00:20:23.560 --> 00:20:24.760
Come on, Kotomi!

00:20:24.760 --> 00:20:25.950
No way!

00:20:25.950 --> 00:20:28.490
We’re going out,
so you have to wear your hat.

00:20:28.490 --> 00:20:30.880
Mi-chan, be careful, it’s dangerous.

00:20:30.880 --> 00:20:31.950
Wait!

00:20:37.810 --> 00:20:41.470
Sheesh, listen to me.

00:20:44.530 --> 00:20:46.890
What are you doing? We’re heading out.

00:20:46.890 --> 00:20:48.110
Papa!

00:20:48.110 --> 00:20:49.580
Irie-kun!

00:20:54.700 --> 00:20:56.300
Here, Papa!

00:20:57.310 --> 00:20:58.980
Thank you, Kotomi.

00:21:00.500 --> 00:21:02.210
Mi-chan wins!

00:21:03.180 --> 00:21:04.240
I keep losing.

00:21:04.850 --> 00:21:08.070
Sheesh, don’t you ever get sick of it?

00:21:09.430 --> 00:21:11.580
Eh, Mi-chan. You have a boy you like?

00:21:11.580 --> 00:21:14.060
Yeah, Yoshiya-kun.

00:21:14.060 --> 00:21:15.690
He gave me some clay.

00:21:15.690 --> 00:21:16.830
Really?

00:21:16.830 --> 00:21:19.550
First, you have to attack!

00:21:19.550 --> 00:21:21.260
Attack?

00:21:22.950 --> 00:21:25.670
For instance, how about writing a love letter?

00:21:25.670 --> 00:21:27.920
Hey, don’t teach her strange things.

00:21:28.930 --> 00:21:30.270
Are you jealous?

00:21:30.270 --> 00:21:31.500
Of course not.

00:21:32.160 --> 00:21:35.690
Kotomi, between Papa and Yoshiya-kun, who do you love more?

00:21:35.690 --> 00:21:37.480
Papa!

00:21:37.480 --> 00:21:38.400
See?

00:21:38.400 --> 00:21:41.360
I’m going to marry Papa after all.

00:21:42.740 --> 00:21:46.840
You can’t! Papa is Mama’s.

00:21:46.840 --> 00:21:48.360
Papa is mine!

00:21:48.360 --> 00:21:51.190
Hey, who’s the jealous one?

00:23:07.360 --> 00:23:08.960
Huh? A preview?

00:23:08.960 --> 00:23:11.790
Hey, this wasn’t the final episode?

00:23:11.790 --> 00:23:13.230
That’s what I thought too.

00:23:13.230 --> 00:23:16.100
Hey, Kotomi! Don’t cling onto Papa so much!

00:23:17.000 --> 00:23:20.070
Papa loves me more than Mama!

00:23:20.070 --> 00:23:21.500
That’s true.

00:23:21.500 --> 00:23:22.680
No way!

00:23:23.330 --> 00:23:24.640
Serves you right!

00:23:26.790 --> 00:23:28.730
Next time on Itazura na Kiss:

00:23:28.730 --> 00:23:30.320
Hello again.

00:23:30.320 --> 00:23:32.770
We’re definitely gonna be happy!
